                <pb facs="0995" n="893" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg893"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/1761: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-10-12T13:00:00+01:00">October 12, 1935—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 12—9:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>697. My 693, October 12, 9 a.m. Above telegram based on information available
                    yesterday. Today I learn that in addition to the French Embassy, the British,
                    German and Belgian Embassies and the Greek and Egyptian Legations have now
                    received instructions and have made oral representations. I understand that with
                    the exception of the Egyptian Legation, which based its representations on the
                    law of nations, all were based upon humanitarian motives. Up to now we were the
                    only Government to make representations as per your 154, October 4, 4 p.m.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Long</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
